---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { url } from '../lib/url'

const tiers = [
  {
    name: 'Open Source',
    price: 'Free',
    period: 'forever',
    tagline: 'The full registry and CLI. No account, no lock-in.',
    cta: { label: 'Get started', href: url('/docs/getting-started'), primary: false },
    features: [
      'outlet CLI (init, add, list, remove, diff, update)',
      'Public registry: all concerns and adapters',
      'Namespace rewriting & environment detection',
      'Self-host your own registry over HTTP',
      'Community support on GitHub',
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'Outlet Cloud',
    price: 'Early access',
    period: 'pricing announced at launch',
    tagline: 'Hosted private registries and team workflows for companies.',
    cta: { label: 'Join early access', href: url('/cloud#early-access'), primary: true },
    highlight: true,
    features: [
      'Everything in Open Source',
      'Hosted private registries for your internal adapters',
      'Team & access management',
      'Drift detection: diff your repo against registry updates',
      'Audit log of installed items across projects',
      'Priority support',
    ],
  },
]
---

<Base title="Pricing — Outlet" description="Outlet is free and open source. Outlet Cloud adds hosted private registries and team workflows.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-center text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Free where it counts. Paid where it scales.</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-zinc-400">
      The registry and CLI are open source, forever. Outlet Cloud is the hosted layer for
      teams that want private registries without running the infrastructure.
    </p>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-14 grid max-w-4xl gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {tiers.map((t) => (
        <div class={`flex flex-col rounded-3xl border p-8 ${t.highlight ? 'border-brand-500/50 bg-gradient-to-b from-brand-500/10 to-ink-900' : 'border-ink-700 bg-ink-900/60'}`}>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{t.name}</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-400">{t.tagline}</p>
          <p class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold text-white">{t.price}</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500">{t.period}</p>
          <ul class="mt-8 flex-1 space-y-3 text-sm text-zinc-300">
            {t.features.map((f) => (
              <li class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="mt-0.5 text-brand-400">✓</span>
                {f}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <a
            href={t.cta.href}
            class={`mt-8 rounded-xl px-6 py-3 text-center font-medium transition ${t.cta.primary ? 'bg-brand-500 text-white hover:bg-brand-600' : 'border border-ink-700 text-zinc-200 hover:border-zinc-500'}`}
          >
            {t.cta.label}
          </a>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-24">
    <h2 class="text-center text-2xl font-bold text-white">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/60 p-6">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-white">Will the open-source CLI stay free?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
          Yes. The CLI, the public registry and every adapter in it are and will remain free.
          Outlet Cloud only charges for the hosted platform: private registries, teams, audit.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/60 p-6">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-white">Do I depend on Outlet at runtime?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
          No. Installed code is copied into your repository and compiled as your own code.
          Cancelling a subscription or uninstalling the CLI breaks nothing.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/60 p-6">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-white">When does Outlet Cloud launch?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-400">
          The open-source MVP is complete (engine, CLI, email concern). Distribution is being
          deployed now; Outlet Cloud follows. Join the early access to be notified first.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
